Guide: Of course. It is said that this mirror can tell right from wrong.
Tourist: How interesting! And what is that carving on the roof?
Guide: That is called chiwen, one of the nine sons of the Chinese dragon.
Tourist: I have never heard of it. Is this palace very old?
Guide: Yes. It was built hundreds of years ago and is an important heritage site.
Tourist: Thank you. I really want to help protect places like this.
Guide: That''s wonderful. Every visitor who cares can make a difference.', '游客请向导介绍一面古镜;向导说这镜子据说能分辨是非;游客又问屋顶上的雕刻;那叫鸱吻,是中国龙的九子之一;宫殿建于数百年前,是重要遗产地;游客想帮忙保护这样的地方;向导说每个用心的游客都能起作用。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the guide say about the old mirror?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It can tell right from wrong.","It is made of gold.","It was bought last year.","It is for sale."]},{"q":"What is the carving on the roof called?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A dragon''s tail.","Chiwen.","A mirror.","A pyramid."]},{"q":"How old is the palace?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Built hundreds of years ago.","Only a few years old.","Built last month.","Nobody knows at all."]},{"q":"What does the tourist want to do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Buy the mirror.","Help protect such places.","Leave at once.","Take the carving home."]},{"q":"What does the guide say about caring visitors?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They cause trouble.","They should stay away.","Each one can make a difference.","They waste money."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U1');
It includes temples, relics, and ancient buildings.
But it also includes customs, dances, and old crafts.
We live with this heritage today and pass it on to the future.
Protecting it is the duty of every one of us.', '文化遗产是我们从过去继承下来的;它包括庙宇、文物和古建筑;但也包括习俗、舞蹈和古老的手工艺;我们今天与这份遗产共存,并把它传给未来;保护它是我们每个人的责任。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where does cultural heritage come from?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["From the future only.","From other planets.","From nowhere.","From the past."]},{"q":"Which of these is part of heritage, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Customs and old crafts.","Only new buildings.","Cars and computers.","Modern roads."]},{"q":"What do we do with this heritage today?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["We throw it away.","We live with it and pass it on.","We sell it abroad.","We hide it forever."]},{"q":"Whose duty is it to protect heritage?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only the government''s.","Only teachers''.","Every one of us.","Only old people''s."]},{"q":"What is the main idea of the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only temples matter.","Heritage is useless.","We should forget the past.","Cultural heritage is broad and worth protecting."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U1');
Student: Sure. We are high school students from seven different countries.
Reporter: That''s amazing. What exactly are you creating?
Student: We are making an app to introduce the mountain to young people.
Reporter: Why did you choose an app?
Student: Because it is a fun and easy way to share its history.
Reporter: Do you do anything besides the app?
Student: Yes, we visit local schools to talk about protecting heritage.', '记者问营地在泰山做什么;学生说他们是来自七个国家的高中生;他们在制作一个向年轻人介绍泰山的应用;选择应用是因为它有趣又容易分享历史;除了应用,他们还去当地学校宣传保护遗产。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where are the students from?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Seven different countries.","Only one city.","Only Egypt.","Nowhere in particular."]},{"q":"What are the students creating?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A new road.","An app about the mountain.","A large temple.","A film about school."]},{"q":"Why did they choose an app?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It is expensive.","Their teacher forced them.","It is a fun, easy way to share history.","Nobody knows."]},{"q":"What else do the students do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["They climb every day.","They sell photos.","They rest all day.","They visit local schools to talk about heritage."]},{"q":"What is the students'' main goal?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To share the mountain''s history with young people.","To build a new dam.","To make money quickly.","To close the mountain."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U1');
First, never touch or damage old relics when you visit them.
Second, learn the stories behind them and share what you know.
Third, join a group of volunteers near you.
Even small actions can help save our treasures.', '这里有三个保护文化遗产的简单方法;第一,参观时绝不触碰或损坏古老文物;第二,了解它们背后的故事并分享;第三,加入身边的志愿者团体;即使微小的行动也能帮助拯救我们的珍宝。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the first piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Take the relics home.","Never touch or damage old relics.","Sell the relics.","Climb on the relics."]},{"q":"What is the second piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Forget the stories.","Keep silent about them.","Learn the stories and share them.","Hide what you know."]},{"q":"What is the third piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Stay home alone.","Buy more tickets.","Build a new wall.","Join a group of volunteers."]},{"q":"How many ways does the passage give?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Three.","One.","Two.","Five."]},{"q":"What does the passage say about small actions?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["They are useless.","They can help save our treasures.","They cost too much.","They cause damage."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U1');
Ben: How much have we collected so far?
Anna: Only half of what we need. The roof is in danger.
Ben: Maybe we could ask different departments to contribute.
Anna: Good idea. We could also invite the public to donate.
Ben: I can write a letter to ask local companies for help.
Anna: Perfect. If we work together, I''m sure we can save it.
Ben: Let''s start today. There is no time to lose.', 'Anna 说委员会要为修庙筹更多钱;Ben 问已筹多少;只筹到一半,屋顶有危险;Ben 建议请各部门捐助;Anna 说也可邀请公众捐款;Ben 愿写信向本地公司求助;两人决定齐心就能拯救它;立刻就动手,刻不容缓。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why does the committee need money?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To build a new road.","To buy a computer.","To repair the old temple.","To take a holiday."]},{"q":"How much have they collected so far?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["All of it.","Nothing at all.","Far too much.","Only half of what they need."]},{"q":"What does Ben suggest first?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Asking different departments to contribute.","Giving up.","Closing the temple.","Selling the temple."]},{"q":"What will Ben do to help?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Climb the roof.","Write a letter to local companies.","Take photos.","Do nothing."]},{"q":"How do they feel about saving the temple?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They think it is hopeless.","They do not care.","They are sure they can if they work together.","They want to wait a year."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U1');
When ancient temples were in danger, one nation asked the world for help.
A committee was set up to limit the damage.
Many countries gave money and sent their best experts.
Together, they proved that great challenges can lead to great solutions.', '有时一个问题对单个国家来说太大;当古庙陷入危险时,一个国家向世界求助;成立了一个委员会以减少损害;许多国家出钱并派出最优秀的专家;他们共同证明,巨大的挑战能带来伟大的解决方案。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"When is a problem too big for one country?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["When it is tiny.","When nobody cares.","When it is already solved.","When it is very large and difficult."]},{"q":"What did one nation do when the temples were in danger?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It asked the world for help.","It did nothing.","It hid the temples.","It sold the temples."]},{"q":"What was the committee set up to do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To build a dam.","To limit the damage.","To collect tickets.","To close the country."]},{"q":"How did many countries help?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They sent nothing.","They only watched.","They gave money and sent experts.","They caused more damage."]},{"q":"What did the countries prove together?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Nothing can be done.","Money is useless.","Temples should be left to fall.","Great challenges can lead to great solutions."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required2', 'U1');

